{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Engine: re-run the séances when a recipe changes",
  "description": "Every curated séance must pass against the real packages and every mutant must fail. The unit tests only check the generated text, so a recipe change needs the real run.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": ["packages/engine/src/seance/recipes/*.ts", "packages/engine/src/seance/generic.ts"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A séance recipe changed. In packages/engine run `npm run build`, then `node scripts/run-seances.mjs <recipe-id>`. The script builds its own scratch folder (npm and a Python virtual environment, pinned to the versions in the committed records) and removes it at the end; set NECROMANCER_SEANCE_SCRATCH to a folder to keep and reuse one, and it writes nothing in the repository. Report the OK/PROBLEM line. OK means the séance passes against the real packages and each mutant fails. If a séance fails, the counterexample is in <scratch>/records/<recipe>.log (the scratch folder is the one NECROMANCER_SEANCE_SCRATCH names, or add --keep to keep the temporary one); it is either a real difference (record it as a known difference and handle it in the replacement) or a mistake in the recipe; decide which before editing. When the recipe is right, run again with --record: that rewrites test/fixtures/seance-runs/<recipe>.json and .log, both tracked. Then run `npm test`."
  }
}
